{
  "abstract": "An explicit binary Turing machine with 196 working states searches for a contradiction in ordinary first-order Peano arithmetic. Lean proves blank-tape nonhalting and that PA proves neither the exact arithmetic halting sentence nor its negation. A refutation compiler connects the PA proof predicate to the literal 392-row table. The axiom command uses a transposed quantifier code and a guarded equality-vacuity clause.",
